WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:06.800
It goes without saying that the SCP Foundation
has a storied history with ancient anomalous

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:08.470
groups of interest.

00:00:08.470 --> 00:00:13.300
From the metal-worshiping Mekhanites, to the
fire-loving Brazen Heart, to even the brutal

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:18.970
empire of the slave-owning Daeva, who swear
allegiance to the dreaded Scarlet King But

00:00:18.970 --> 00:00:24.290
perhaps the most dangerous and downright disgusting
of these groups are the flesh-worshipping,

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:28.810
disease-loving, body-warping Sarkicists.

00:00:28.810 --> 00:00:33.450
The Sarkicists believe in returning humanity
to a nightmarish primordial state.

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:40.050
They utilize anomalies to achieve this goal,
such as the horrible SCP-610, also known as

00:00:40.050 --> 00:00:45.870
The Flesh That Hates, a disease that converts
human beings into mindless beasts of twisted

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:49.489
flesh, driven to spread their disease further
and further.

00:00:49.489 --> 00:00:54.649
The Sarkics were once a world superpower,
controlling much of modern-day Russia and

00:00:54.649 --> 00:01:00.969
eastern Europe from the holy capital of Adytum,
a city ahead of its time, with towering blood-red

00:01:00.969 --> 00:01:07.759
temples, wide, winding roads, and the Castle
of Grand Karcist Ion, an immense, blistering

00:01:07.759 --> 00:01:12.380
red and gold structure that was as beautiful
as it was imposing.

00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:17.829
It would only make sense that the former area
of the Sarkic empire would host some of the

00:01:17.829 --> 00:01:20.850
most ghastly of the Sarkic anomalies.

00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:25.659
It should not be forgotten that while the
Sarkics are a Group of Interest for the SCP

00:01:25.659 --> 00:01:30.959
Foundation, they are first and foremost a
religion – one with ancient practices of

00:01:30.959 --> 00:01:32.670
blood and human sacrifice.

00:01:32.670 --> 00:01:37.811
While the SCP Foundation is famed for its
containment procedures, when it comes to the

00:01:37.811 --> 00:01:43.280
likes of actual deities entities, containment
isn’t quite as straightforward.

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:47.669
The standard “put it in a box until it stops
trying to get out” technique just won’t

00:01:47.669 --> 00:01:53.009
cut it – the deities require specific practices
that sometimes go against the core values

00:01:53.009 --> 00:01:56.000
of Secure, Contain, Protect.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:02.039
Take SCP-2845 for example, this entity, known
as “The Deer” is a being that requires

00:02:02.039 --> 00:02:07.700
an intense, deadly, and specific ritual to
keep it properly contained.

00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:12.819
The SCP Foundation even had to outsource help
in containing this anomaly.

00:02:12.819 --> 00:02:18.959
Anomalies such as these place The SCP Foundation
at a crossroads of action or inaction, and

00:02:18.959 --> 00:02:23.880
when this issue is combined with a Sarkic
anomaly that could bring catastrophic results

00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:28.180
should containment fail, they need to make
the difficult choice of letting the anomaly

00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:33.540
stay where it is - without intervention - for
the safety of the world.

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:39.439
This nightmare started in the year 1916 , during
the battle of Transylvania of the First World

00:02:39.439 --> 00:02:40.439
War.

00:02:40.439 --> 00:02:45.909
As bullets flew and the smell of smoke pervaded
the noses of the scared soldiers, blood-lusting

00:02:45.909 --> 00:02:51.189
beasts were waiting their time to strike,
staking behind the unnaturally curved trunks

00:02:51.189 --> 00:02:54.810
of the trees that lived in the nearby Hoia
Forest.

00:02:54.810 --> 00:02:59.549
Soldiers, armed with weapons and tactical
armor, were quickly and brutally attacked

00:02:59.549 --> 00:03:04.400
and consumed by entities that would be known
as the ‘Pale Men.’

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:08.829
At the time, not much was known about these
‘Pale Men,’ and they were believed to

00:03:08.829 --> 00:03:14.470
be a myth among the local populace meant to
scare invading soldiers from stepping on Romanian

00:03:14.470 --> 00:03:15.470
land.

00:03:15.470 --> 00:03:21.709
But, when 244 people go randomly missing in
a single night, with no obvious signs of death,

00:03:21.709 --> 00:03:27.440
no bodies ever being found, and reports of
Pale Men dashing through trenches and within

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:33.420
the surrounding Hoia forest, the SCP Foundation
would surely have to intervene.

00:03:33.420 --> 00:03:39.219
This would not occur until 1919, however,
as World War One raged on, diverting Foundation

00:03:39.219 --> 00:03:43.079
attention away from these mysterious deaths.

00:03:43.079 --> 00:03:48.749
Agents Fredrick Harper and Reece Gorman, posing
as military officials and local law enforcement,

00:03:48.749 --> 00:03:52.830
began to speak with the locals around the
Hoia forest and the surviving soldiers.

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:57.989
While shell shock rocked the soldiers with
guilt and terror, Gorman was able to ascertain

00:03:57.989 --> 00:04:02.889
that the soldier’s stories of the Pale Men
were too consistent to be a falsehood created

00:04:02.889 --> 00:04:04.140
out of stress.

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:11.079
The pale men were described as living vampires,
more bat than human, and deadly fast, appearing

00:04:11.079 --> 00:04:17.150
in quick flashes before dragging the unsuspecting
victims to their untimely deaths within the

00:04:17.150 --> 00:04:18.289
Hoia Forest.

00:04:18.289 --> 00:04:23.020
Meanwhile, Agent Gorman spoke with members
of a village within the Hoia Forest near the

00:04:23.020 --> 00:04:24.020
battle site.

00:04:24.020 --> 00:04:27.210
Their demeanor was cold, which was expected.

00:04:27.210 --> 00:04:32.400
He was an outsider, speaking rudimentary Romanian
in an obviously foreign tongue.

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:36.639
The village people claimed ignorance, declaring
that they never heard stories of pale men

00:04:36.639 --> 00:04:39.170
and did not subscribe to fairy tales.

00:04:39.170 --> 00:04:44.140
Gorman, realizing he was unwanted, nearly
cut his losses before the elder of the village

00:04:44.140 --> 00:04:45.400
stopped him.

00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:51.310
This elder, an old man draped in hand-knit
scarves and red silks, invited the agent into

00:04:51.310 --> 00:04:54.250
his home and gave him the truth.

00:04:54.250 --> 00:04:56.990
These villagers were followers of Sarkicism.

00:04:56.990 --> 00:05:01.860
The home of the elder was decorated with Sarkic
glyphs and paintings detailing the stories

00:05:01.860 --> 00:05:07.900
of Yaldabaoth – the primary god of the Sarkics
– battling Mekhane – the legendary Broken

00:05:07.900 --> 00:05:08.900
God.

00:05:08.900 --> 00:05:14.650
On a lectern sat scolls and dusty tomes detailing
Sarkic history – from former kings to stories

00:05:14.650 --> 00:05:18.430
of battles that were waged against the Mekhanites
and Daevites.

00:05:18.430 --> 00:05:23.800
The elder explained that there was a Sarkic
god within the Hoia Forest, known as “The

00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:29.050
Mother” who sends out her children to feed
and help her grow ever larger.

00:05:29.050 --> 00:05:33.440
The village worshipped The Mother and tried
their best to keep her at bay by conducting

00:05:33.440 --> 00:05:37.190
ritual sacrifices to her and her brood.

00:05:37.190 --> 00:05:42.570
However, the advent of World War One led to
difficulties in continuing their rituals as

00:05:42.570 --> 00:05:47.440
they were living in an active warzone and
the Mother’s children and their hunger were

00:05:47.440 --> 00:05:53.879
impossible to control, leading to the unfortunate
deaths of the soldiers.

00:05:53.879 --> 00:05:58.219
Agent Gorman was eventually able to convince
the elder to show them where The Mother resided

00:05:58.219 --> 00:06:03.150
– a temple, superficially resembling other
Eastern Orthodox monasteries.

00:06:03.150 --> 00:06:08.140
But this was no house of God that you or I
would recognize.

00:06:08.140 --> 00:06:15.889
On the lower level, it contained an ancient
beast, starving for blood and sacrifice.

00:06:15.889 --> 00:06:23.200
This place soon became designated SCP-2191,
otherwise known as The Dracula Factory.

00:06:23.200 --> 00:06:25.819
New containment procedures were quickly enacted.

00:06:25.819 --> 00:06:30.009
Twenty armed guards were placed around the
temple, with strict orders to dispatch any

00:06:30.009 --> 00:06:32.700
entity that exits the structure.

00:06:32.700 --> 00:06:37.069
Standard containment procedures for anomalous
buildings were enacted as well, preventing

00:06:37.069 --> 00:06:43.720
all non-Foundation personnel from entering
SCP-2191 and authorizing the use of lethal

00:06:43.720 --> 00:06:45.639
force when necessary.

00:06:45.639 --> 00:06:51.169
Access to SCP-2191 has allowed Foundation
biologists to research the entities that were

00:06:51.169 --> 00:06:53.409
known as the Pale Men.

00:06:53.409 --> 00:06:58.259
These creatures were found to be genetically
human, but with a variety of alterations that

00:06:58.259 --> 00:07:01.330
should have resulted in fatalities.

00:07:01.330 --> 00:07:06.240
These entities were subsequently designated
as SCP-2191-1.

00:07:06.240 --> 00:07:12.879
SCP-2191-1 entities appear to be more bat
than human, with large, conical ears that

00:07:12.879 --> 00:07:20.030
end in sharp tips, upturned noses, and the
ability to communicate via echolocation.

00:07:20.030 --> 00:07:26.740
This echolocation ability comes in handy,
as SCP-2191-1 are completely blind – their

00:07:26.740 --> 00:07:32.230
eyes have recessed into their skulls and a
layer of skin has grown over them.

00:07:32.230 --> 00:07:38.009
The entities also lack pigmentation, leaving
them starkly pale, appearing to be made more

00:07:38.009 --> 00:07:40.949
of porcelain than flesh and bone.

00:07:40.949 --> 00:07:47.389
These entities are predators, solely hunting
living human beings – ignoring human cadavers

00:07:47.389 --> 00:07:49.759
or any non-human animal.

00:07:49.759 --> 00:07:54.259
They hunt by spreading through the Hoia Forest
and chasing their victims.

00:07:54.259 --> 00:08:00.030
Once caught, SCP-2191 entities will inject
their victims with a paralytic agent by stabbing

00:08:00.030 --> 00:08:03.659
them with a sharp bone that has grown from
their wrists.

00:08:03.659 --> 00:08:09.509
They will then unhinge their jaws, allowing
a leech-like entity to exit their mouths and

00:08:09.509 --> 00:08:13.750
begin the feeding process by latching onto
the victim's neck.

00:08:13.750 --> 00:08:21.500
This leech, designated as SCP-2191-2, will
first inject the body with digestive enzymes,

00:08:21.500 --> 00:08:27.280
converting organ, muscle, and bone into liquid
before consuming the resulting fluids.

00:08:27.280 --> 00:08:32.180
The feeding process can last anywhere from
20 to 50 minutes, depending on the size of

00:08:32.180 --> 00:08:33.420
its prey.

00:08:33.420 --> 00:08:37.480
These are highly skilled and sophisticated
predators, and while they lack the higher

00:08:37.480 --> 00:08:42.530
intelligence of non-anomalous humans, they
make up for it in ruthless ferocity.

00:08:42.530 --> 00:08:47.380
It would only make sense that the Foundation
would enact strict containment procedures

00:08:47.380 --> 00:08:50.030
to avoid the loss of human life.

00:08:50.030 --> 00:08:55.000
But while these containment methods worked
for a time, a series of anomalous events connected

00:08:55.000 --> 00:09:00.200
to SCP-2191 transpired over the next 70 years.

00:09:00.200 --> 00:09:02.850
The first event was in late September of 1932.

00:09:02.850 --> 00:09:10.410
The Ierissos earthquake devastated the Chalkidiki
peninsula of Greece, leaving houses crumbled,

00:09:10.410 --> 00:09:14.900
civilians homeless, and causing 490 reported
casualties.

00:09:14.900 --> 00:09:20.230
Surveys of the damage conducted by the Greek
Government found that 126 people who lived

00:09:20.230 --> 00:09:23.350
in the affected areas could not be accounted
for.

00:09:23.350 --> 00:09:28.380
The question now arises, where are these missing
people?

00:09:28.380 --> 00:09:35.220
Seven years later in 1939, this time in Turkey,
the Erzincan earthquake struck the country,

00:09:35.220 --> 00:09:40.200
resulting in the catastrophic deaths of approximately
33,000 people.

00:09:40.200 --> 00:09:45.140
Among the survivors, reports of a “great
serpent” were given from all who witnessed

00:09:45.140 --> 00:09:46.140
the event.

00:09:46.140 --> 00:09:51.230
The Foundation then intervened, posing as
members of an international disaster recovery

00:09:51.230 --> 00:09:52.540
agency.

00:09:52.540 --> 00:09:57.030
Reports from the locals remained the same
– a great serpent, a deep red and black

00:09:57.030 --> 00:10:03.580
in color and incomprehensively massive, casting
dark shadow miles long, rose from the ground

00:10:03.580 --> 00:10:09.090
at the onset of the earthquake and writhed
in the air as the Earth shook.

00:10:09.090 --> 00:10:14.580
For a period of three years, nothing related
to SCP-2191 transpired and the Foundation

00:10:14.580 --> 00:10:17.490
believed that the anomaly had gone dormant.

00:10:17.490 --> 00:10:21.840
That was until an earthquake struck Vrancea,
Romania in 1940.

00:10:21.840 --> 00:10:27.260
While casualties were low compared to the
earthquake in Turkey, reports from local survivors

00:10:27.260 --> 00:10:33.480
had repeated claims that “pale men” attacked
the fleeing people as the earthquake occurred,

00:10:33.480 --> 00:10:37.590
chasing after them and tackling them, never
to be seen again.

00:10:37.590 --> 00:10:43.600
With a large-scale event like this and potential
witnesses to anomalous beings, the SCP Foundation

00:10:43.600 --> 00:10:48.430
was risking a Broken Masquerade Scenario should
this information spread.

00:10:48.430 --> 00:10:54.350
Broken Masquerade scenarios are considered
an XK Class scenario by the SCP Foundation

00:10:54.350 --> 00:10:58.830
and as such, they employed a media blackout
and had newspapers state that the witnesses

00:10:58.830 --> 00:11:02.890
of these vampire attacks were nothing but
superstition.

00:11:02.890 --> 00:11:09.010
In March 1953 in Turkey, the Yenice-Gönen
earthquake led to the deaths of over 1,000

00:11:09.010 --> 00:11:10.010
people.

00:11:10.010 --> 00:11:15.290
The Foundation, once again posing as members
of an international disaster recovery agency,

00:11:15.290 --> 00:11:20.600
interviewed survivors and attempted to find
any connection to the preceding events.

00:11:20.600 --> 00:11:26.520
Reports from survivors again told a consistent
story, they witnessed the "arm of a blood-red

00:11:26.520 --> 00:11:32.150
octopus" rupture from the earth when the quake
began , behaving similar to the “great serpent”

00:11:32.150 --> 00:11:36.850
writhing in the sky, and reported that "pale
men" were seen attacking survivors in the

00:11:36.850 --> 00:11:40.190
night as they searched for places to sleep.

00:11:40.190 --> 00:11:45.200
These sightings of pale men persisted for
over a month after the earthquake before amnestics

00:11:45.200 --> 00:11:47.040
could be distributed.

00:11:47.040 --> 00:11:50.570
Another event occurred in March of 1977 in
Romania.

00:11:50.570 --> 00:11:56.300
It was a similar story to all the others,
with over 1500 civilians dying as a result

00:11:56.300 --> 00:12:01.140
of the Vrancea earthquake and 800 civilians
being declared missing.

00:12:01.140 --> 00:12:05.230
Foundation officials embedded in the Romanian
government were told that reports of "pale

00:12:05.230 --> 00:12:10.640
men" and tendrils pulling victims beneath
the ground began to surface, leading to media

00:12:10.640 --> 00:12:14.800
blackouts and amnestic distribution as panic
spread throughout the region.

00:12:14.800 --> 00:12:18.380
The Foundation couldn’t figure out what
was causing these events.

00:12:18.380 --> 00:12:26.490
When they began instituting the containment
procedures around SCP-2191, no SCP-2191-1

00:12:26.490 --> 00:12:30.200
entities were able to exit the temple without
being quickly dispatched.

00:12:30.200 --> 00:12:36.130
So, how were these events occurring, especially
in areas so far away from the Hoia forest?

00:12:36.130 --> 00:12:39.880
Could it be that the large creature seen breaching
the Earth was responsible?

00:12:39.880 --> 00:12:44.680
The Foundation decided to return to the village
that originally told them about the temple

00:12:44.680 --> 00:12:47.150
to interview their elder once more.

00:12:47.150 --> 00:12:50.820
Doctor Judith Low was given permission to
conduct the interview.

00:12:50.820 --> 00:12:56.150
She was a senior employee of the SCP Foundation
and had multiple doctorates in Sarkic History

00:12:56.150 --> 00:13:01.450
and Sarkic Anthropology – her expertise
in the subject was unmatched.

00:13:01.450 --> 00:13:06.110
Doctor Low had written multiple studies on
the Sarkic culture and understood that only

00:13:06.110 --> 00:13:09.950
one thing satiates Sarkic Gods: Blood.

00:13:09.950 --> 00:13:14.870
With this knowledge in mind, Doctor Low met
with Draga Negrescu, the current elder of

00:13:14.870 --> 00:13:16.060
the village.

00:13:16.060 --> 00:13:21.580
Draga was an old woman, wrapped in the red
silks and scarves as the previous elder.

00:13:21.580 --> 00:13:26.330
Doctor Low began the interview and jumped
immediately to the subject, asking Draga what

00:13:26.330 --> 00:13:28.600
she could tell her about the temple.

00:13:28.600 --> 00:13:33.520
Draga replied, stating that the temple was
the home of what they called “The Mother.”

00:13:33.520 --> 00:13:37.990
The Mother was not unlike a queen bee, as
she sends her drones out to collect blood

00:13:37.990 --> 00:13:40.940
much like bees collect nectar.

00:13:40.940 --> 00:13:46.000
Draga continued, stating that her village
acted as the beekeepers to The Mother, helping

00:13:46.000 --> 00:13:50.590
the hive flourish and stay full before the
SCP Foundation intervened.

00:13:50.590 --> 00:13:55.230
Draga expressed that it was imperative that
they would be allowed to continue their sacred

00:13:55.230 --> 00:13:57.720
duty of satiating The Mother.

00:13:57.720 --> 00:14:01.710
Doctor Low needed more information on who
exactly The Mother was.

00:14:01.710 --> 00:14:06.500
Draga Negrescu told her that The Mother was
once a princess and the daughter of a Sarkic

00:14:06.500 --> 00:14:10.440
Blood Empress in Adytum, the ancient Sarkic
capital.

00:14:10.440 --> 00:14:15.800
She was a strikingly beautiful girl, wearing
the finest of clothes and had long, dark red

00:14:15.800 --> 00:14:20.590
hair – a trait common to those with ancient,
royal Sarkic bloodlines.

00:14:20.590 --> 00:14:24.700
When she walked through the streets of Adytum,
all eyes turned toward her.

00:14:24.700 --> 00:14:29.910
The Grand Karcist Ion was struck by her beauty
and kidnapped the princess, claiming her as

00:14:29.910 --> 00:14:30.990
his own.

00:14:30.990 --> 00:14:32.570
She became his mistress.

00:14:32.570 --> 00:14:38.810
While she first hated her position, she slowly
grew to worship Grand Karcist Ion as a god.

00:14:38.810 --> 00:14:43.560
While Grand Karcist Ion is seen as a deity
now, he was not during his reign as the King

00:14:43.560 --> 00:14:45.550
of the Sarkic Empire.

00:14:45.550 --> 00:14:49.000
The princess begged to bear Ion’s children
as a result.

00:14:49.000 --> 00:14:54.550
She was blessed by the Grand Karcist and was
planted in the Koia Forest to grow large and

00:14:54.550 --> 00:14:55.550
wide.

00:14:55.550 --> 00:15:00.180
Ion commanded the princess to bear as many
children as she could muster, and she did.

00:15:00.180 --> 00:15:05.460
The princess birthed Ion’s children – the
pale ones – for all of eternity and would

00:15:05.460 --> 00:15:08.200
let them feed as Ion would want.

00:15:08.200 --> 00:15:12.450
Draga stated that she and her village are
no different than the pale men, as they were

00:15:12.450 --> 00:15:16.100
tasked with keeping The Mother fed and satisfied.

00:15:16.100 --> 00:15:18.280
Draga then let slip this chilling remark:

00:15:18.280 --> 00:15:22.040
“The Mother and the land are now one.

00:15:22.040 --> 00:15:28.480
Her earthen womb swells and soon she will
rupture.

00:15:28.480 --> 00:15:33.400
All around you is tinder for the Gods.”

00:15:33.400 --> 00:15:38.200
It seems as though the Foundation’s containment
efforts led to the deadly earthquakes and

00:15:38.200 --> 00:15:40.530
deaths of thousands of people.

00:15:40.530 --> 00:15:44.801
By stopping the practices of this village
to contain The Mother through ritual, they

00:15:44.801 --> 00:15:49.400
had potentially caused an XK-Class end of
the world scenario.

00:15:49.400 --> 00:15:52.690
One question remained, though: Where is The
Mother?

00:15:52.690 --> 00:15:59.800
An investigation into the tunnel systems located
below SCP-2191 would lead to the answer.

00:15:59.800 --> 00:16:04.770
Mobile Task Force units that specialized in
underground exploration, such as the Mole

00:16:04.770 --> 00:16:09.770
Rats, were sent to the tunnel system below
the temple, armed with weapons to dispatch

00:16:09.770 --> 00:16:14.090
any loose SCP-2191-1 entities.

00:16:14.090 --> 00:16:20.280
These agents discovered a grisly sight, a
massive, writhing mass below SCP-2191.

00:16:20.280 --> 00:16:26.680
Researchers, believing Draga’s story, ascertained
that this was The Mother, and designated it

00:16:26.680 --> 00:16:29.850
as SCP-2191-3.

00:16:29.850 --> 00:16:36.630
This entity is a massive, blood-red organism
buried deep beneath the earth where SCP-2191

00:16:36.630 --> 00:16:37.820
stands.

00:16:37.820 --> 00:16:43.280
The true size of the entity has proven entirely
impossible to measure, but root-like appendages

00:16:43.280 --> 00:16:46.870
have been found to extend throughout the tunnels
below the Earth.

00:16:46.870 --> 00:16:52.330
These appendages were found to secrete a toxic,
highly corrosive acid.

00:16:52.330 --> 00:17:01.050
SCP-2191-3 uses this fluid to create tunnels,
which explains the odd tunnels below SCP-2191-2.

00:17:01.050 --> 00:17:07.539
Measurements place the area SCP-2191 spread
to approximately 660,000 square kilometers

00:17:07.539 --> 00:17:09.970
under the Balkan Penninsula.

00:17:09.970 --> 00:17:18.290
For comparison’s sake, SCP-3000 - the amnestic-producing
eel god, Ananatashesha - is a measly 900 kilometers

00:17:18.290 --> 00:17:19.970
in length at maximum.

00:17:19.970 --> 00:17:27.319
With that in mind, now we can see the gargantuan
problem the SCP Foundation was dealing with.

00:17:27.319 --> 00:17:33.499
SCP-2191-3 is sapient – meaning it has an
innate sense of understanding and self-awareness

00:17:33.499 --> 00:17:42.299
– and exerts control over SCP-2191-1 and
SCP-2191-2 organisms via the release of complex

00:17:42.299 --> 00:17:44.070
pheromones.

00:17:44.070 --> 00:17:50.280
SCP-2191-1 entities act as feeder drones for
SCP-2191-3.

00:17:50.280 --> 00:17:55.049
It has since been discovered that civilians,
native to several isolated villages in the

00:17:55.049 --> 00:18:02.289
vicinity of Hoia Forest, have actively provided
human sacrifices to SCP-2191 as a means of

00:18:02.289 --> 00:18:06.879
minimizing the seismic activity that occurs
when it is famished – and this worked to

00:18:06.879 --> 00:18:11.780
satiate the entity and prevent further damage
to the Earth and its people.

00:18:11.780 --> 00:18:16.240
The Foundation now stood at the crossroad
between active containment and allowing the

00:18:16.240 --> 00:18:20.510
people who knew and understood the anomaly
to contain it themselves.

00:18:20.510 --> 00:18:26.259
The Foundation motto is Secure, Contain, Protect,
however, if they allow Draga Negrescu and

00:18:26.259 --> 00:18:31.440
her village to continue their sacrifices,
they will be unable to fulfill any of those

00:18:31.440 --> 00:18:36.340
core values, but SCP-2191 will not be wreaking
havoc.

00:18:36.340 --> 00:18:39.009
This dilemma led to the involvement of the
O5 Council.

00:18:39.009 --> 00:18:44.320
A joint statement from them reads: There are
some who wish to believe that the Foundation

00:18:44.320 --> 00:18:50.760
has never, nor will ever, cater to the designs
and desires of an anomalous entity.

00:18:50.760 --> 00:18:56.250
Foundation efforts to contain SCP-2191 are
now thought to have inadvertently led to the

00:18:56.250 --> 00:19:00.750
deaths of approximately 40,000 over 45 years.

00:19:00.750 --> 00:19:03.610
The obvious choice would be to neutralize
the threat.

00:19:03.610 --> 00:19:04.610
And we've tried.

00:19:04.610 --> 00:19:09.799
The number of civilian and Foundation casualties
being well beyond acceptable numbers.

00:19:09.799 --> 00:19:13.660
In order to contain the larger threat, we
must allow it to feed.

00:19:13.660 --> 00:19:17.100
We are aware of the offense caused by this
procedure.

00:19:17.100 --> 00:19:20.980
This is not the first time, nor will it be
the last, that the Foundation has been forced

00:19:20.980 --> 00:19:24.620
to commit a lesser evil in the prevention
of a greater one.

00:19:24.620 --> 00:19:29.840
We do believe that, in the end, our current
method is the most preferable - with regards

00:19:29.840 --> 00:19:31.860
to both ethics and efficiency.

00:19:31.860 --> 00:19:39.830
We are fully aware that every sacrifice feeds
SCP-2191-3, allowing it and its brood to thrive.

00:19:39.830 --> 00:19:44.799
But we are not about to sacrifice the entire
Balkan Peninsula to neutralize that threat.

00:19:44.799 --> 00:19:46.080
Not yet.

00:19:46.080 --> 00:19:51.070
It was clear that the SCP Foundation had no
choice but to allow the villagers who lived

00:19:51.070 --> 00:19:56.490
around SCP-2191 and The Mother to continue
their practices.

00:19:56.490 --> 00:20:01.559
Upon their involvement, there was catastrophe
after catastrophe that would only stop once

00:20:01.559 --> 00:20:06.440
the correct people – Draga Negrescu and
her villagers – could return to their way

00:20:06.440 --> 00:20:08.429
of life and end the madness.

00:20:08.429 --> 00:20:12.249
A final containment procedure was ordered
as a result.

00:20:12.249 --> 00:20:17.710
The SCP Foundation would maintain surveillance
operations via the use of closed-circuit security

00:20:17.710 --> 00:20:19.740
cameras, and drone footage.

00:20:19.740 --> 00:20:24.230
All personnel of the SCP Foundation would
be prohibited from directly interfering with

00:20:24.230 --> 00:20:30.850
SCP-2191 or the ritual practices of communities
within the vicinity of the Hoia Forest, which

00:20:30.850 --> 00:20:35.910
include blood or human sacrifices to SCP-2191.

00:20:35.910 --> 00:20:41.409
Exploration of SCP-2191 would only be allowed
by remote-controlled drones.

00:20:41.409 --> 00:20:46.649
Lethal force is only authorized should SCP-2191
or any of the creatures that live beneath

00:20:46.649 --> 00:20:48.530
it breach containment.

00:20:48.530 --> 00:20:52.940
Should the Foundation fail in upholding the
ritual practices that keep The Mother at bay,

00:20:52.940 --> 00:20:53.940
well…

00:20:53.940 --> 00:20:56.030
Draga Negrescu said it best:

00:20:56.030 --> 00:20:59.789
All around them is tinder for the Gods.

00:20:59.789 --> 00:21:07.759
Now go check out “SCP-2783 - Silent Lamentations
of a Clockwork Goddess” and “SCP-1348

00:21:07.759 --> 00:21:10.440
- Inner Sanctum” for more fascinating anomalous
locations!

